            "text": "An efficient and exact Python program to compute the sum of Euclidean distances over all ordered pairs:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load vectors from the current directory\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors_secondary.npy\")\n\n    # Cast to float64 to ensure high numerical precision\n    X = vectors.astype(np.float64)\n\n    # Compute Gram matrix (pairwise dot products)\n    G = X @ X.T\n\n    # Squared Euclidean distance: ||u - v||^2 = ||u||^2 + ||v||^2 - 2*(u . v)\n    sq_norms = np.diag(G)\n    D2 = sq_norms[:, None] + sq_norms[None, :] - 2.0 * G\n\n    # Numerical safeguard for tiny negative values due to floating-point rounding\n    np.maximum(D2, 0.0, out=D2)\n\n    # Compute Euclidean distances\n    D = np.sqrt(D2)\n\n    # Diagonal entries are exactly zero\n    np.fill_diagonal(D, 0.0)\n\n    total = float(np.sum(D))\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
